        <img src="/images/poster_physicalai_2.jpg" alt="Lecture Poster" class="w-full rounded-2xl border border-slate-900 my-6 object-cover shadow-2xl" />
        
        <p>
          In our June 20 lecture, we introduced the core concepts of Embodied Intelligence and Physical AI and their latest development trends. However, as we look closer at recent industry dynamics, a major technical paradigm shift is taking place: <strong>from language-centric VLA (Vision-Language-Action) models to physical-prediction-centric World Models and World Action Models.</strong>
        </p>
        
        <p>
          This lecture will focus on this technical paradigm shift, discussing why traditional VLA models face bottlenecks, what fundamental changes World Models bring, and how these changes are impacting the industry in 2026.
        </p>

        <hr class="border-slate-900 my-8" />

        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white border-l-4 border-blue-500 pl-3">Date & Time</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-slate-300">
          <li><strong>Pacific Time (PDT)</strong>: July 18 (Saturday) 5:30 PM – 6:30 PM</li>
          <li><strong>Eastern Time (EDT)</strong>: July 18 (Saturday) 8:30 PM – 9:30 PM</li>
          <li><strong>Beijing Time (CST)</strong>: July 19 (Sunday) 8:30 AM – 9:30 AM</li>
        </ul>

        <hr class="border-slate-900 my-8" />

        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white border-l-4 border-blue-500 pl-3">Lecture Outline</h3>
        
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <div>
            <h4 class="font-semibold text-white">Introduction (0–6 mins)</h4>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 mt-1">
              The historical transition of AI from the "digital world" to the "physical world." Why 2025–2026 is considered a critical inflection point for Physical AI. The core focus: the paradigm evolution from VLA to World Models.
            </p>
          </div>
          
          <div>
            <h4 class="font-semibold text-white">Part 1: Paradigm Shift from VLA to World Models (6–20 mins)</h4>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 mt-1">
              Advantages and limitations of traditional VLA models. Why the industry is looking for new technical paradigms. Core concepts and background of World Models. How World Action Models (WAMs) break through VLA limitations.
            </p>
          </div>
          
          <div>
            <h4 class="font-semibold text-white">Part 2: Technological Breakthroughs in 2026 Physical AI (20–40 mins)</h4>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 mt-1">
              Latest updates on NVIDIA Cosmos 3 and World Foundation Models. Advantages of World Action Models in generalization and physical prediction. Real-world deployment of major humanoid robotics platforms (Figure, Tesla Optimus, Boston Dynamics Atlas, etc.). Joint applications of digital twins and Physical AI.
            </p>
          </div>
          
          <div>
            <h4 class="font-semibold text-white">Part 3: Challenges, Status & Future Trends (40–52 mins)</h4>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 mt-1">
              The biggest remaining challenges for Physical AI today. Integration trends between VLA and World Models. Development path predictions for 2026–2030. Practical implications for businesses and creators.
            </p>
          </div>
          
          <div>
            <h4 class="font-semibold text-white">Summary & Live Q&A (52–60 mins)</h4>
          </div>
        </div>

        <hr class="border-slate-900 my-8" />

        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white border-l-4 border-blue-500 pl-3">How to Join</h3>
